    "discussionSummary": "Majority D: one LB plus three backend services is what binds three URL paths on one hostname to three functions. B voters wanted direct function exposure, which cannot share yourcompany.com paths.",
    "conceptSummary": "Path-based routing to three Cloud Functions behind one load balancer.",
    "correctRationale": "To serve three different paths on the same hostname you need path-based routing — the external HTTP(S) load balancer's URL map does that, sending each path to a different serverless backend (one function each). Directly exposed functions get their own URLs and cannot share the domain paths.",
