        "user": "Popa",
        "text": "Selected Answer: C. Option B: The permissions of the service account’s predefined role have changed. If the permissions of the service account's role were altered, it could indeed result in a 403 Permission Denied error. However, such changes are typically deliberate and should be documented. If you have not altered the permissions, this might be less likely. Option C: The service account key has been rotated but... (3 votes)"
